<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Likelihood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Observation model for Bayesian inference: p(data | sim(theta)). Points at the observation holding the data and specifies the noise family + scale. `name` is the noise family (default Normal); `source` uses the same referencing as `Observation.source`, so the observed data can come from this experiment's integration, an empirical network measure, or a runtime-bound array — one flexible hook, no data-loading path of its own." .
