# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode#nested
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode#nested> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode#nested> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode#nested> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode#nested> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "nested (AlgorithmCompositionMode)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode#nested> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The included algorithm runs as a full inner loop on EACH outer iteration, re-converging before the outer update rules are applied. Use when the inner algorithm maintains an invariant the outer one would otherwise perturb — e.g. FIC holding the E-I working point (mean S_e = 0.25) while EIB retunes per-edge coupling. The outer update's validity depends on that invariant, so the inner loop must re-settle it between every outer step." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/AlgorithmCompositionMode#nested> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "nested" .
