# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "from_previous (SweepSeeding)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Each point is seeded from the final state of the preceding point, so the trajectory follows the solution branch as the swept parameter changes quasi-statically. Forces sequential, order-dependent execution (emitted as a scan, not a vmap). Used to reach a working point by slowly ramping a parameter (e.g. global coupling) and, with sweep_direction, to expose hysteresis / multistability. Sweep-granularity analogue of InitialStateMethod.from_branch." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "from_previous" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "independent (SweepSeeding)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Each point is initialised independently from the model's initial values (a cold start), so points are order-independent and may be evaluated in parallel (see parallel_mode). Default; today's behaviour." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "independent" .
