# https://w3id.org/tvbo/neuroml/proximal
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/neuroml/proximal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/neuroml/proximal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/neuroml/point3DWithDiam> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/neuroml/proximal> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Point on a _segment_ closest to the soma. Note, the proximal point can be omitted, and in this case is defined as being the point _fractionAlong between the proximal and _distal_ point of the _parent_, i.e. if _fractionAlong = 1 (as it is by default) it will be the _distal on the parent, or if _fractionAlong = 0, it will be the proximal point. If between 0 and 1, it is the linear interpolation between the two points."@en .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/neuroml/proximal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/neuroml> .
