<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingDependentAuxiliaryRecording> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Recording (via `output` or `record: true`) a derived/auxiliary variable whose equation reads a coupling input, with the auxiliary aligned to the state it is recorded alongside. Under the default per-step (frozen) coupling the recorded auxiliary carries the step-start coupling — one integration step behind the recorded post-step state — so exact state/coupling alignment requires per-stage coupling evaluation."@en .
