<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/StateVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/surrogate_of> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0005272> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "Derivative(V, t)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "d*tau*(I*gamma - V**3*f + V**2*e + V*g + V*local_coupling + W*alpha + c_glob*gamma)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "V_G2D is the first state-variable of the Generic 2-Dimensional Oscillator model, that can be associated with membrane potentials and sodium activation (FitzHugh, 1961)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0005272> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "V (Generic2dOscillator state variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/V> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "V" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/StateVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/surrogate_of> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0005272> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "Derivative(W, t)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "d*(V**2*c + V*b - W*beta + a)/tau" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "W_G2D is the second state-variable of the Generic 2-Dimensional Oscillator model, that can be associated with accommodation and refractoriness and considered to represent potassium activation, sodium inactivation, or both (FitzHugh, 1961)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0005272> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "W (Generic2dOscillator state variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Generic2dOscillator/state_variables/W> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "W" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Parameter> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Slope parameter of the state-variable 'x_GL', representing the inverse of the relaxation time" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma> <http://schema.org/defaultValue> "-10.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "gamma (GenericLinear parameter)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Slope parameter of the state-variable 'x_GL', representing the inverse of the relaxation time.\n\nNote: The ‘minus’ sign for the self-connections, scaled by 'gamma_GL', guarantees that the nodes have a stable equilibrium point (ref)." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/parameters/gamma> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "gamma" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/StateVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "Derivative(x, t)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "c_glob + gamma*x + local_coupling*x" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "State-variable of the Generic Linear model" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "x (GenericLinear state variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/GenericLinear/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "x" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/dynamic
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/dynamic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/dynamic> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Parameter> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/dynamic> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Threshold dynamics: 0 (default) -> theta tracks x (TVB display hack); >0 -> theta relaxes to its own coupling input." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/dynamic> <http://schema.org/defaultValue> "0.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/dynamic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dynamic (Hopfield parameter)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/dynamic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "dynamic" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Parameter> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The slow time-scale for threshold calculus :math:`\\\\theta`, state-variable of the model" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT> <http://schema.org/defaultValue> "5.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "tauT (Hopfield parameter)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The slow time-scale for threshold calculus :math:`\\\\theta`, state-variable of the model." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/tauT> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "tauT" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Parameter> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The fast time-scale for potential calculus :math:`x`, state-variable of the model" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux> <http://schema.org/defaultValue> "1.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "taux (Hopfield parameter)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The fast time-scale for potential calculus :math:`x`, state-variable of the model." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/parameters/taux> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "taux" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/StateVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "Derivative(theta, t)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "Piecewise(((c_glob1 - theta)/tauT, dynamic > 0), ((c_glob0 - x)/taux, True))" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Slow state variable at node i" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "theta (Hopfield state variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/theta> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "theta" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/x
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/StateVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/x> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "Derivative(x, t)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/x> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "(c_glob0 - x)/taux" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "x (Hopfield state variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/Hopfield/state_variables/x> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "x" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/DerivedVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "sigma_y0_1" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "2.0*nu_max/(exp(r*(-J*a_1*y0 + v0)) + 1.0)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Sigmoid function that transforms the average membrane potential of the PCs populations (y0) into an average firing rate to the excitatory interneurons EINs." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sigma_y0_1 (JansenRit derived variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "sigma_y0_1" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/DerivedVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "sigma_y0_3" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "2.0*nu_max/(exp(r*(-J*a_3*y0 + v0)) + 1.0)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Sigmoid function that transforms the average membrane potential of the PCs populations (y0) into an average firing rate to the inhibitory interneurons IINs." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sigma_y0_3 (JansenRit derived variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y0_3> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "sigma_y0_3" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/DerivedVariable> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/lhs> "sigma_y1_y2" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/rhs> "2.0*nu_max/(exp(r*(v0 - y1 + y2)) + 1.0)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Sigmoid function that transforms the average membrane potential of the interneurons populations (y1-y2)\ninto an average firing rate to the PCs." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "sigma_y1_y2 (JansenRit derived variable)" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/JansenRit/derived_variables/sigma_y1_y2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "sigma_y1_y2" .
