<https://w3id.org/tvbo/graph_generators/WeightShuffle/parameters/preserve> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Which structural property to hold fixed under permutation. Only `binary_mask` is implemented: keep the {0, nonzero} pattern and permute the weight values among their existing positions, so density and topology stay fixed while the weight-to-edge assignment is randomised. Any other value is rejected — a null model that silently controlled a different property than the one asked for would invalidate the comparison it exists to support." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/graph_generators/WeightShuffle/parameters/preserve> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "preserve (WeightShuffle parameter)" .
