# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/HemodynamicObservation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BOLD fMRI observation model using a Gamma-shaped hemodynamic response function. Provides a simpler, unimodal HRF shape." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BOLD_Gamma" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_gamma/parameters/TR> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BOLD fMRI observation model identical to BOLD_TVB's HRF+Volterra forward model, but with the HRF convolution and TR subsampling fused into a single strided convolution (strided_convolve): the convolution is evaluated only at the retained [stride::stride] output samples, avoiding the full-length FFT. Byte-identical to a direct full 'valid' convolution + subsample; equal to the FFT path to FFT roundoff (~1e-12 float64 / ~1e-6 float32); ~70x cheaper with no FFT buffer." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BOLD_HRF_strided" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_hrf_strided/parameters/TR> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/HemodynamicObservation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BOLD fMRI observation model using the canonical double-gamma hemodynamic response function (Glover 1999). Standard HRF used in most fMRI analysis packages (SPM, FSL, AFNI)." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BOLD_MixtureOfGammas" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_mixture_of_gammas/parameters/TR> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/HemodynamicObservation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BOLD fMRI observation model that computes the hemodynamic response at each source location and spatially averages within brain regions using a parcellation mapping. Produces per-region BOLD signals suitable for comparison with parcellated empirical data." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BOLD_RegionROI" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_region_roi/parameters/hrf_length> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_tvb
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_tvb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_tvb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_tvb> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "BOLD fMRI observation model using the Balloon-Windkessel hemodynamic model. Transforms neural activity into simulated BOLD signal via convolution with a hemodynamic response function (First Order Volterra kernel), followed by a nonlinear Volterra transformation." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_tvb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "BOLD_TVB" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_tvb> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/bold_tvb/parameters/TR> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Forward solution for scalp electroencephalography. Projects source neural activity through a lead field (gain) matrix to electrode locations on the scalp. If no precomputed gain is available, uses a single-sphere analytic approximation (Sarvas 1987, Eq. 12). Supports re-referencing: common average, single-electrode, or ideal reference-free recording." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EEG" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg/parameters/conductivity> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/eeg/parameters/reference_electrode> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/global_average
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/global_average> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/global_average> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/global_average> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Spatial mean across all network nodes at each sampling period. Reduces spatial dimension to a single global signal per state variable." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/global_average> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GlobalAverage" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/ieeg
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/ieeg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/ieeg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/ieeg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Forward solution for intracranial/stereoelectroencephalography (SEEG). Projects source activity through a lead field matrix to implanted depth electrode contacts. Uses the same single-sphere analytic formula as scalp EEG (Sarvas 1987, Eq. 12), but with electrode positions inside the brain volume." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/ieeg> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "iEEG" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/ieeg> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/ieeg/parameters/conductivity> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/meg
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/meg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/meg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/meg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Forward solution for magnetoencephalography. Projects source neural activity through a lead field matrix to MEG sensor locations using oriented gradiometers. If no precomputed gain is available, uses the single-sphere analytic formula (Sarvas 1987, Eq. 25) for the magnetic field produced by current dipoles in a conducting sphere." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/meg> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MEG" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/meg> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/meg/parameters/permeability> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/raw
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/raw> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/raw> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/raw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Records all state variables at every integration step without any transformation. Identity passthrough of the full simulation state." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/raw> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Raw" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/spatial_average
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/spatial_average> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/spatial_average> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/spatial_average> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Computes spatially averaged signals within regions defined by a spatial mask (node-to-region assignment). The mask assigns each node to a region index, and the output is the mean signal per region." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/spatial_average> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SpatialAverage" .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/spatial_average> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hasParameter> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/spatial_average/parameters/spatial_mask> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/subsample
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/subsample> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/subsample> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/subsample> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Temporal decimation of selected state variables. Records every N-th integration step without any averaging or smoothing." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/subsample> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SubSample" .
# 
# https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/temporal_average
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/temporal_average> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/temporal_average> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/tvbo/Observation> .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/temporal_average> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Running temporal mean over a sliding window of configurable length. Returns one averaged sample per period." .
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/observation_models/temporal_average> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TemporalAverage" .
